IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc22-verdicts`

-- ccc22-tests-verdicts.l4 -- tests for ccc22-verdicts.l4 (sections 660 to 669.3). Expected values are written from the text, beside the assertion. Arguments are in the order of each function's GIVEN lines.

§ `Sections 660 to 661`

-- 660: args: the complete commission of the offence charged is proved, the evidence establishes an attempt.
#ASSERT `s 660 the accused may be convicted of the attempt` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 660 the accused may be convicted of the attempt` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the complete offence is proved: the "where" gate fails (ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 660 the accused may be convicted of the attempt` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no attempt established
#ASSERT `s 660 the accused may be convicted of the attempt` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 661(1) entitled to be acquitted: args: an attempt is charged, the evidence establishes the complete offence.
#ASSERT `s 661(1) the accused is entitled to be acquitted` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "the accused is not entitled to be acquitted"
#ASSERT `s 661(1) the accused is entitled to be acquitted` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 661(1) the accused is entitled to be acquitted` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 661(1) jury: args: an attempt is charged, the evidence establishes the complete offence, the judge has discharged the jury and directed an indictment for the complete offence.
#ASSERT `s 661(1) the jury may convict the accused of the attempt` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 661(1) the jury may convict the accused of the attempt` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless the judge ... discharges the jury from giving a verdict"
#ASSERT `s 661(1) the jury may convict the accused of the attempt` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a "where" gate (ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 661(1) the jury may convict the accused of the attempt` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 661(1) judge: args: an attempt is charged, the evidence establishes the complete offence.
#ASSERT `s 661(1) the judge presiding at the trial may discharge the jury from giving a verdict and direct that the accused be indicted for the complete offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 661(1) the judge presiding at the trial may discharge the jury from giving a verdict and direct that the accused be indicted for the complete offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 661(1) the judge presiding at the trial may discharge the jury from giving a verdict and direct that the accused be indicted for the complete offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 661(2): args: the accused is convicted under section 661.
#ASSERT `s 661(2) the accused is liable to be tried again for the offence the accused was charged with attempting to commit` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "is not liable to be tried again"
#ASSERT `s 661(2) the accused is liable to be tried again for the offence the accused was charged with attempting to commit` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 662`

-- 662(1): args: the count is a count in an indictment.
#ASSERT `s 662(1) a count in an indictment is divisible` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 662(1) a count in an indictment is divisible` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 662(1)(a): args: the offence charged includes another offence, the included offence is proved.
#ASSERT `s 662(1)(a) the accused may be convicted of the included offence that is proved` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 662(1)(a) the accused may be convicted of the included offence that is proved` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "of an offence so included that is proved"
#ASSERT `s 662(1)(a) the accused may be convicted of the included offence that is proved` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the "where" gate: no included offence (ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 662(1)(a) the accused may be convicted of the included offence that is proved` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 662(1)(b): args: the offence charged includes another offence, the evidence establishes an attempt to commit the included offence.
#ASSERT `s 662(1)(b) the accused may be convicted of an attempt to commit the included offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 662(1)(b) the accused may be convicted of an attempt to commit the included offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 662(1)(b) the accused may be convicted of an attempt to commit the included offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 662(2): args: the offence the count charges, what the evidence proves.
#ASSERT `s 662(2) the jury may find the accused not guilty of first degree murder but guilty of second degree murder or an attempt to commit second degree murder` `first degree murder` `s 662(2) second degree murder` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 662(2) the jury may find the accused not guilty of first degree murder but guilty of second degree murder or an attempt to commit second degree murder` `first degree murder` `s 662(2) an attempt to commit second degree murder` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 662(2) the jury may find the accused not guilty of first degree murder but guilty of second degree murder or an attempt to commit second degree murder` `first degree murder` `s 662(2) first degree murder` EQUALS NOTHING   -- first degree murder is proved: the clause is silent
#ASSERT `s 662(2) the jury may find the accused not guilty of first degree murder but guilty of second degree murder or an attempt to commit second degree murder` `first degree murder` `s 662(2) none of these` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 662(2) the jury may find the accused not guilty of first degree murder but guilty of second degree murder or an attempt to commit second degree murder` `second degree murder` `s 662(2) second degree murder` EQUALS NOTHING   -- "For greater certainty and without limiting the generality of subsection (1)": a count of another kind is not decided here
#ASSERT `s 662(2) the jury may find the accused not guilty of first degree murder but guilty of second degree murder or an attempt to commit second degree murder` `manslaughter` `s 662(2) second degree murder` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 662(3) lesser finding: args: the count charges murder, the evidence proves manslaughter or infanticide, the evidence proves murder.
#ASSERT `s 662(3) the jury may find the accused not guilty of murder but guilty of manslaughter or infanticide` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 662(3) the jury may find the accused not guilty of murder but guilty of manslaughter or infanticide` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a "where" gate: no count of murder
#ASSERT `s 662(3) the jury may find the accused not guilty of murder but guilty of manslaughter or infanticide` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 662(3) the jury may find the accused not guilty of murder but guilty of manslaughter or infanticide` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- murder is proved
-- 662(3) no other offence: args: the count charges murder, subsection (4) applies.
#ASSERT `s 662(3) the jury may on that count find the accused guilty of any other offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "shall not on that count find the accused guilty of any other offence"
#ASSERT `s 662(3) the jury may on that count find the accused guilty of any other offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "Subject to subsection (4)"
#ASSERT `s 662(3) the jury may on that count find the accused guilty of any other offence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no count of murder
-- 662(4): args: the count charges the murder of a child or infanticide, the evidence proves an offence under section 243, the evidence proves murder or infanticide.
#ASSERT `s 662(4) the jury may find the accused not guilty of murder or infanticide but guilty of an offence under section 243` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 662(4) the jury may find the accused not guilty of murder or infanticide but guilty of an offence under section 243` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 662(4) the jury may find the accused not guilty of murder or infanticide but guilty of an offence under section 243` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 662(4) the jury may find the accused not guilty of murder or infanticide but guilty of an offence under section 243` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 662(5): args: the count charges an offence under section 220, 221 or 236 arising out of the operation of a conveyance, the evidence proves that offence, the evidence proves an offence under section 320.13.
#ASSERT `s 662(5) the accused may be convicted of an offence under section 320.13` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 662(5) the accused may be convicted of an offence under section 320.13` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the offence charged is proved: the clause is silent ("for greater certainty")
#ASSERT `s 662(5) the accused may be convicted of an offence under section 320.13` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 662(5) the accused may be convicted of an offence under section 320.13` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 662(5.1): args: the count charges an offence under subsection 263.1(1), the evidence proves that offence, the evidence proves an included offence.
#ASSERT `s 662(5.1) the accused may be found guilty of the offence that is proved` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 662(5.1) the accused may be found guilty of the offence that is proved` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 662(5.1) the accused may be found guilty of the offence that is proved` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 662(5.1) the accused may be found guilty of the offence that is proved` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 662(6): args: the count charges an offence under paragraph 98(1)(b) or 348(1)(b), the evidence proves that offence, the evidence proves the offence under, respectively, paragraph 98(1)(a) or 348(1)(a).
#ASSERT `s 662(6) the accused may be convicted of an offence under that latter paragraph` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 662(6) the accused may be convicted of an offence under that latter paragraph` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a "where" gate (ruling (b)); subsection (6) carries no "for greater certainty"
#ASSERT `s 662(6) the accused may be convicted of an offence under that latter paragraph` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 662(6) the accused may be convicted of an offence under that latter paragraph` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 662(7): args: the count charges an offence under subsection 320.1001(1), the evidence proves that offence, the evidence proves an included offence.
#ASSERT `s 662(7) the accused may be found guilty of the offence that is proved` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 662(7) the accused may be found guilty of the offence that is proved` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 662(7) the accused may be found guilty of the offence that is proved` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 662(7) the accused may be found guilty of the offence that is proved` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 663`

-- 663: args: a female person is charged with infanticide, the evidence establishes that she caused the death of her child, it establishes (a) not fully recovered, it establishes (b) balance of mind disturbed, it establishes that the act or omission was not wilful.
#ASSERT `s 663 the female person may be convicted of infanticide` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 663 the female person may be convicted of infanticide` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- only (a) is established: the evidence does not establish (a) AND (b)
#ASSERT `s 663 the female person may be convicted of infanticide` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- only (b) is established
#ASSERT `s 663 the female person may be convicted of infanticide` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- both (a) and (b) are established: the section gives no such conviction
#ASSERT `s 663 the female person may be convicted of infanticide` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless the evidence establishes that the act or omission was not wilful"
#ASSERT `s 663 the female person may be convicted of infanticide` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not charged with infanticide
#ASSERT `s 663 the female person may be convicted of infanticide` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the evidence does not establish that she caused the death

§ `Sections 664 to 669 -- Previous convictions`

-- 664: args: the indictment is in respect of an offence for which, by reason of previous convictions, a greater punishment may be imposed.
#ASSERT `s 664 the section bars the indictment from containing any reference to previous convictions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 664 the section bars the indictment from containing any reference to previous convictions` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 665 what the text shows` EQUALS "[Repealed, 1995, c. 22, s. 3]"
-- 666: args: the accused adduces evidence of good character, the prosecutor adduces the evidence in answer, a verdict has been returned.
#ASSERT `s 666 the prosecutor may adduce evidence of the previous conviction of the accused` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 666 the prosecutor may adduce evidence of the previous conviction of the accused` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a "where" gate: no evidence of good character
#ASSERT `s 666 the prosecutor may adduce evidence of the previous conviction of the accused` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "before a verdict is returned"
#ASSERT `s 666 the prosecutor may adduce evidence of the previous conviction of the accused` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not "in answer thereto"
#ASSERT `s 666 the prosecutor may adduce evidence of the previous conviction of the accused` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the "where" gate is read first
-- 667(1)(a): args: the certificate sets out the conviction etc. with reasonable particularity, proof that the accused is the offender referred to, the signer.
#ASSERT `s 667(1)(a) the certificate is evidence that the accused or defendant was so convicted, so discharged or so convicted and sentenced or found guilty and sentenced` TRUE TRUE `s 667(1)(a)(i) the person who made the conviction, order for the discharge or finding of guilt` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 667(1)(a) the certificate is evidence that the accused or defendant was so convicted, so discharged or so convicted and sentenced or found guilty and sentenced` TRUE TRUE `s 667(1)(a)(ii) the clerk of the court in which the conviction, order for the discharge or finding of guilt was made` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 667(1)(a) the certificate is evidence that the accused or defendant was so convicted, so discharged or so convicted and sentenced or found guilty and sentenced` TRUE TRUE `s 667(1)(a)(iii) a fingerprint examiner` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 667(1)(a) the certificate is evidence that the accused or defendant was so convicted, so discharged or so convicted and sentenced or found guilty and sentenced` TRUE TRUE `s 667(1)(a) some other signer` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "if it is signed by (i), (ii) or (iii)"
#ASSERT `s 667(1)(a) the certificate is evidence that the accused or defendant was so convicted, so discharged or so convicted and sentenced or found guilty and sentenced` TRUE FALSE `s 667(1)(a)(i) the person who made the conviction, order for the discharge or finding of guilt` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "on proof that the accused or defendant is the offender"
#ASSERT `s 667(1)(a) the certificate is evidence that the accused or defendant was so convicted, so discharged or so convicted and sentenced or found guilty and sentenced` FALSE TRUE `s 667(1)(a)(i) the person who made the conviction, order for the discharge or finding of guilt` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 667(1)(a) the certificate is evidence that the accused or defendant was so convicted, so discharged or so convicted and sentenced or found guilty and sentenced` FALSE FALSE `s 667(1)(a) some other signer` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 667(1)(b): args: evidence that the fingerprints are the same, evidence to the contrary.
#ASSERT `s 667(1)(b) the fingerprint evidence is proof that the accused or defendant is the offender referred to in that certificate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 667(1)(b) the fingerprint evidence is proof that the accused or defendant is the offender referred to in that certificate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "in the absence of evidence to the contrary"
#ASSERT `s 667(1)(b) the fingerprint evidence is proof that the accused or defendant is the offender referred to in that certificate` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 667(1)(c): args: the certificate is a certificate of a fingerprint examiner stating the comparison.
#ASSERT `s 667(1)(c) the certificate is evidence of the statements contained in it without proof of the signature or the official character of the person appearing to have signed it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 667(1)(c) the certificate is evidence of the statements contained in it without proof of the signature or the official character of the person appearing to have signed it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 667(1)(d): args: the certificate, the number of the Form.
#ASSERT `s 667(1)(d) the certificate may be in the Form` `s 667(1)(d) a certificate under subparagraph (a)(iii)` 44 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 667(1)(d) the certificate may be in the Form` `s 667(1)(d) a certificate under paragraph (c)` 45 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 667(1)(d) the certificate may be in the Form` `s 667(1)(d) a certificate under subparagraph (a)(iii)` 45 EQUALS NOTHING   -- the text does not say a certificate may be in no other form
#ASSERT `s 667(1)(d) the certificate may be in the Form` `s 667(1)(d) a certificate under paragraph (c)` 44 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 667(1)(d) the certificate may be in the Form` `s 667(1)(d) some other certificate` 44 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 667(2): args: the document is a copy of the summary conviction or discharge signed by the person who made it or the clerk, proof that the accused is the offender referred to.
#ASSERT `s 667(2) the copy is evidence of the conviction or discharge under section 730 of the accused or defendant` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 667(2) the copy is evidence of the conviction or discharge under section 730 of the accused or defendant` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "on proof that the accused or defendant is the offender"
#ASSERT `s 667(2) the copy is evidence of the conviction or discharge under section 730 of the accused or defendant` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 667(2.1): args: summary conviction proceedings, the name is similar, evidence to the contrary.
#ASSERT `s 667(2.1) the similarity of name is evidence that the defendant is the offender referred to in the certificate or the copy` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 667(2.1) the similarity of name is evidence that the defendant is the offender referred to in the certificate or the copy` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "in the absence of evidence to the contrary"
#ASSERT `s 667(2.1) the similarity of name is evidence that the defendant is the offender referred to in the certificate or the copy` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not summary conviction proceedings
#ASSERT `s 667(2.1) the similarity of name is evidence that the defendant is the offender referred to in the certificate or the copy` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 667(3): args: a certificate under (1)(a)(iii) or (1)(c) is produced against the accused, the court has given leave.
#ASSERT `s 667(3) the accused may require the attendance of the person who signed the certificate for the purposes of cross-examination` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 667(3) the accused may require the attendance of the person who signed the certificate for the purposes of cross-examination` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "with leave of the court": the "if"-kind gate fails (a grant: NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 667(3) the accused may require the attendance of the person who signed the certificate for the purposes of cross-examination` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 667(4): args: the certificate is one issued under (1)(a)(iii) or (1)(c), the party has given reasonable notice with a copy.
#ASSERT `s 667(4) the subsection bars receiving the certificate in evidence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 667(4) the subsection bars receiving the certificate in evidence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the "unless" is met
#ASSERT `s 667(4) the subsection bars receiving the certificate in evidence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 667(5): args: designated by the Minister for the purposes of section 667.
#ASSERT `s 667(5) the person is a fingerprint examiner` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 667(5) the person is a fingerprint examiner` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "means a person designated as such"
#ASSERT `s 668 and s 669 what the text shows` EQUALS "668 and 669 [Repealed, 1995, c. 22, s. 4]"

§ `Sections 669.1 to 669.3`

-- 669.1(1): args: the plea was taken by the judge, court or provincial court judge who has not commenced to hear evidence, the other has jurisdiction to try the accused.
#ASSERT `s 669.1(1) the judge, court or provincial court judge has jurisdiction for the purpose of the hearing and adjudication` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 669.1(1) the judge, court or provincial court judge has jurisdiction for the purpose of the hearing and adjudication` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- evidence has begun to be heard: the "Where" condition fails
#ASSERT `s 669.1(1) the judge, court or provincial court judge has jurisdiction for the purpose of the hearing and adjudication` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not one "having jurisdiction to try the accused or defendant"
#ASSERT `s 669.1(1) the judge, court or provincial court judge has jurisdiction for the purpose of the hearing and adjudication` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 669.1(2): args: who adjourns, the offence is punishable on summary conviction.
#ASSERT `s 669.1(2) the person may adjourn the proceedings at any time before or after the plea is taken` `s 669.1(2) a court, judge or provincial court judge having jurisdiction to try the accused or defendant` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 669.1(2) the person may adjourn the proceedings at any time before or after the plea is taken` `s 669.1(2) a clerk or other proper officer of the court` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 669.1(2) the person may adjourn the proceedings at any time before or after the plea is taken` `s 669.1(2) a justice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 669.1(2) the person may adjourn the proceedings at any time before or after the plea is taken` `s 669.1(2) a justice` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "in the case of an offence punishable on summary conviction, any justice"
#ASSERT `s 669.1(2) the person may adjourn the proceedings at any time before or after the plea is taken` `s 669.1(2) someone else` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the list is not closed
-- 669.2(1): args: the tribunal, the accused is being tried by it and the judge etc. dies or is unable to continue, the other has jurisdiction.
#ASSERT `s 669.2(1) the proceedings may be continued before another judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person` `s 669.2(1)(a) a judge or provincial court judge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 669.2(1) the proceedings may be continued before another judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person` `s 669.2(1)(b) a justice or other person who is, or is a member of, a summary conviction court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 669.2(1) the proceedings may be continued before another judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person` `s 669.2(1)(c) a court composed of a judge and jury` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 669.2(1) the proceedings may be continued before another judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person` `s 669.2(1)(a) a judge or provincial court judge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the judge neither dies nor is unable to continue: a "where" gate (ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 669.2(1) the proceedings may be continued before another judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person` `s 669.2(1)(a) a judge or provincial court judge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the other person must be one "who has jurisdiction to try the accused or defendant"
#ASSERT `s 669.2(1) the proceedings may be continued before another judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person` `s 669.2(1) some other tribunal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 669.2(2): args: a verdict was rendered or an adjudication was made.
#ASSERT `s 669.2(2) the judge before whom the proceedings are continued must impose the punishment or make the order authorized by law without further election by the accused` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 669.2(2) the judge before whom the proceedings are continued must impose the punishment or make the order authorized by law without further election by the accused` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the duty is "Where a verdict was rendered ... or an adjudication was made"
-- 669.2(3): args: the trial was commenced but no adjudication was made or verdict rendered, the trial is before a judge and jury.
#ASSERT `s 669.2(3) the judge before whom the proceedings are continued must commence the trial again as if no evidence on the merits had been taken` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 669.2(3) the judge before whom the proceedings are continued must commence the trial again as if no evidence on the merits had been taken` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "Subject to subsections (4) and (5)": a jury trial is governed by subsection (4)
#ASSERT `s 669.2(3) the judge before whom the proceedings are continued must commence the trial again as if no evidence on the merits had been taken` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a verdict or adjudication was made
#ASSERT `s 669.2(3) the judge before whom the proceedings are continued must commence the trial again as if no evidence on the merits had been taken` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 669.2(4): args: a jury trial was commenced with no adjudication or verdict, the course.
#ASSERT `s 669.2(4) the judge before whom the proceedings are continued may take the course without further election by the accused` TRUE `s 669.2(4) continue the trial` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 669.2(4) the judge before whom the proceedings are continued may take the course without further election by the accused` TRUE `s 669.2(4) commence the trial again as if no evidence on the merits had been taken` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 669.2(4) the judge before whom the proceedings are continued may take the course without further election by the accused` TRUE `s 669.2(4) some other course` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the list is not closed
#ASSERT `s 669.2(4) the judge before whom the proceedings are continued may take the course without further election by the accused` FALSE `s 669.2(4) continue the trial` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the "If" gate fails (a grant: NOTHING)
-- 669.2(5) deemed: args: the trial is continued under subsection (4), the evidence was adduced before a judge referred to in paragraph (1)(c).
#ASSERT `s 669.2(5) the evidence is deemed to have been adduced before the judge before whom the trial is continued` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 669.2(5) the evidence is deemed to have been adduced before the judge before whom the trial is continued` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 669.2(5) the evidence is deemed to have been adduced before the judge before whom the trial is continued` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 669.2(5) again: args: the trial is continued under subsection (4), the prosecutor and the accused consent.
#ASSERT `s 669.2(5) any part of that evidence may be adduced again before the judge before whom the trial is continued` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 669.2(5) any part of that evidence may be adduced again before the judge before whom the trial is continued` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "if the prosecutor and the accused consent": the "if" gate fails (a grant: NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 669.2(5) any part of that evidence may be adduced again before the judge before whom the trial is continued` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a "where" gate (ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 669.2(5) any part of that evidence may be adduced again before the judge before whom the trial is continued` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 669.3: args: a court, judge or provincial court judge is conducting a trial and is appointed to another court, the trial has been completed.
#ASSERT `s 669.3 the judge or provincial court judge continues to have jurisdiction in respect of the trial` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 669.3 the judge or provincial court judge continues to have jurisdiction in respect of the trial` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 669.3 the judge or provincial court judge continues to have jurisdiction in respect of the trial` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "until its completion"
